From 2cdee83be040ef56db19f04703ab4c889e7f5a8c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: vpavlin <vaclav@status.im>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 06:21:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Lanes view: days down the side, one column per calendar or
 per field value (mobile + desktop)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Third Frequencies-driven Scala extension: a "Lanes" view next to month,
week and day. Rows are 14 days from the selected day (‹ › step a week),
columns are the shown calendars or, with "By <field>", the values of an
enum field across those calendars, so a promoter can see one column per
venue or per status. Lane order is stable: calendars in list order; field
values in schema order, then values only seen on events, then "—" for
events without the field. Cells list events by start time with the clash
and RSVP marks; tapping a date opens that day, tapping an event opens it.
The field filter and hidden calendars apply as in the other views.

Logic in mobile/src/lib/lanes.ts (buildLanes / laneOf), mirrored in
CalendarView.qml. Tests: mobile/test/lanes.test.mjs (10 cases incl. a
weekly residency and unknown values), added to `npm test`. The QML harness
renders the view by calendar and by the Status field (shots 14/15). The
mobile view switcher's buttons are slightly narrower to fit five modes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
